{
  "_comment": "SPINE-1 conformance corpus — D1 ratification fix 2 (2026-07-01): PROVE cross-tier numeric + collation determinism byte-for-byte. General arithmetic uses IEEE-754 double IDENTICALLY on both tiers + a canonical ECMAScript serializer; money.* uses EXACT decimal (BigInteger/BigInt), never IEEE (no rounding — exact-or-fail-closed); all string ops are ORDINAL / code-unit (locale-independent, no Unicode normalization). The no-normalization case uses composed U+00E9 vs decomposed U+0065 U+0301; the substring cases mix composed U+00FC / U+00DF with a decomposed haystack — all BMP (single UTF-16 unit) so the two canonical writers agree code-unit-for-code-unit.",
